    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM8AAAABKEaHJQ",
      "title": "[CONTINGENCY] sep/119: Soneium Minato rollback of batcher + unsafe block signer",
      "author": "Wazabie",
      "number": 1589,
      "body": "Contingency rollback for the Soneium Minato sequencer + batcher cutover in #1565, the Sepolia twin of the mainnet rollback in #1588. Kept as a separate PR and merged only if it is needed.\n\n`sep/119` restores Sony's batcher `0xF0AB0441c8f4B89b561aE685B98c6aD5175e0CAB` and unsafe block signer `0x55930859CD7003F32A2ba171297408476532E535` (the live values before `sep/117`) on the Minato `SystemConfigProxy`, signed by the Sepolia FoundationUpgradeSafe, which stays the SystemConfig owner. The proposer (`sep/116`) has no rollback.\n\nIt is pinned to FoundationUpgradeSafe nonce 84, shared with the foundation approval of `sep/118` (fee vaults), so only one of the two can execute: `sep/118` is executed only once the cutover is confirmed, and if the rollback executes instead, `sep/118` moves up by one nonce and is re-signed. The status `CANCELLED (CONTINGENCY TASK, SIGN AS NEEDED)` keeps it out of the stacked simulation. It is simulated on its own, with state overrides for the post-`sep/117` owner, batcher and signer.\n\nThe calldata is `sep/117`'s with Sony's two addresses swapped in, checked byte for byte and decoded with `cast`. The standalone simulation passes, and the hashes in VALIDATION.md come from it.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-22T16:25:58Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 226,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM8AAAABKESCmA",
      "title": "[CONTINGENCY] eth/088: Soneium Mainnet rollback of batcher + unsafe block signer",
      "author": "Wazabie",
      "number": 1588,
      "body": "Contingency rollback for the Soneium Mainnet sequencer + batcher cutover in #1566. Kept as a separate PR and merged only if it is needed, same as the Ink rollback in #1493.\n\n`eth/088` restores Sony's batcher `0x6776BE80dBAda6A02B5F2095cF13734ac303B8d1` and unsafe block signer `0x7c2Bd59ee2a2C7391c9A240132f26071e9546262` (the live values before `eth/085`) on the Soneium `SystemConfigProxy`, signed by the FoundationUpgradeSafe, which stays the SystemConfig owner. The proposer has no rollback: the OPE proposer (`eth/084`) keeps working whichever party runs the sequencer and batcher.\n\nIt is pinned to FoundationUpgradeSafe nonce 82, so it can be signed ahead of the Nov 19 ceremony and executed within minutes. That nonce is shared with the foundation approval of `eth/086` (fee vaults), so only one of the two can execute. `eth/086` should be executed only once the cutover is confirmed. If the rollback executes instead, `eth/086` and every later FUS task (`eth/087`) move up by one nonce and are re-signed. The status is `CANCELLED (CONTINGENCY TASK, SIGN AS NEEDED)` so `fetch-tasks.sh` leaves it out of the stacked simulation, where the shared nonce would otherwise fail the nonce check. It is simulated on its own, with state overrides for the post-`eth/085` owner, batcher and signer.\n\nThe calldata is `eth/085`'s with Sony's two addresses swapped in, checked byte for byte and decoded with `cast`. The standalone simulation passes, and the hashes in VALIDATION.md come from it.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-22T16:16:04Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 226,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM8AAAABI3cQpg",
      "title": "fix(template): fork L2 pre-flight 5 blocks behind the reported head",
      "author": "Wazabie",
      "number": 1581,
      "body": "Fixes the intermittent `stacked_simulation_eth` failures on main since #1564 ([CI alert thread](https://oplabs-pbc.slack.com/archives/C03N11M0BBN/p1792153643217549)).\r\n\r\n**Cause** `SetL1SplitterConfig` (eth/076, eth/079) and `SetFeeVaultConfig` (eth/080) dry-run on an L2 fork of `https://mainnet.unichain.org` taken at `latest`. That endpoint is load-balanced: one backend reports a head that the backend serving the next request does not have yet, so the fork reads empty state. \r\n\r\n**Fix** Both templates fork `L2_FORK_HEAD_LAG = 5` blocks behind `eth_blockNumber`. The pre-flight still sees live state, about 5s old. Pinned regression harnesses override `_createL2Fork` and are unaffected. Signed calldata and hashes don't change.\r\n\r\n**Verification** `just simulate-stack eth` passes locally for eth/074–080, and every domain/message hash matches its VALIDATION.md.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-16T14:41:26Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-19T03:21:23Z",
      "additions": 39,
      "deletions": 9
    },
